# `version` must match `pyproject.toml`; `scripts/generate_soup_tables.py
# --check` (run by tests/compliance/test_soup_evidence.py) fails if it does
# not.  `date-released` is added when a version is tagged and removed again on
# the next development bump — the same check refuses a release date on a
# pre-release version, because a pre-release does not have one.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "MADDENING: Modular Automatic Differentiation and Data-Enhanced Neural-network INteracting Graph"
type: software
version: 0.4.0.dev0
license: LGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/Microrobotics-Simulation-Framework/MADDENING"
abstract: >
  A JAX-based modular simulation framework for multi-physics.
  MADDENING provides a functional-state graph architecture for
  composing, coupling, and differentiating physics simulations
  with automatic differentiation and neural surrogates.
authors:
  - family-names: Roy
    given-names: Nicholas Ehsan
keywords:
  - simulation
  - multi-physics
  - JAX
  - automatic differentiation
  - lattice Boltzmann
  - neural surrogates
  - microrobotics
